test_logger_*.log
test_logger_nested_dir/
test_diff_view_*.txt
test_*.log

# === Functional-test venv + Python cache (created by `zig build functional-test`) ===
.venv-func/
.pytest_cache/
tests/functional/__pycache__/
tests/functional_ui/__pycache__/
tests/functional_android/__pycache__/
# tests/platform_gates.py lives at the tests/ root, not inside a suite dir,
# and is imported by both suites' conftest.py — so its bytecode cache lands
# in tests/__pycache__/, which the three lines above do not cover.
tests/__pycache__/
# scripts/vm_guest_client.py is imported by the probe and the benchmark, so
# running either leaves this one behind.
scripts/__pycache__/

# === WebView2 NuGet headers + loader (downloaded by CI's
# "Stage WebView2 + integrate vcpkg + install ripgrep (Windows)" step;
# 1.0.2651.64. Re-staged on every Windows CI run from the .nupkg zip;
# the .dll + .lib are runtime link inputs for pabrik-desktop.exe) ===
/src/apps/desktop_app/platform/windows/
# The full path is ignored rather than individual files so the
# auto-created staging directory is also skipped (the directory gets
# recreated by the CI script on every Windows run; git would otherwise
# try to track an empty dir).
#
# Exception: webview_stub.c is the dev-box fallback (no MSVC + WebView2)
# no-op C stub — see build.zig's `.windows =>` else branch + the doc
# comment at the top of that file. We commit it so the no-stub-build
# path always works on a fresh checkout (otherwise the
# `zig build pabrik-desktop` step on a Windows dev box without MSVC +
# WebView2 fails with "file not found" because the .c source is
# missing).
!/src/apps/desktop_app/platform/windows/webview_stub.c
# Exception: guard_tables_stub.c provides the 5 CFG/XFG guard symbols
# nothing else in the link defines (see build.zig's real-WebView2
# branch + the doc comment at the top of that file). Committed for
# the same reason as webview_stub.c.
!/src/apps/desktop_app/platform/windows/guard_tables_stub.c

